profile: minimodel.short-term-memory.v7
updated_utc: 2026-07-02T18:20:00Z
current_state:
  - MiniModel.org is a Rust-first metadata, verifier, and future peer-to-peer tiny model package exchange workspace.
  - Source options are user-owned local files/lists, user-triggered Hugging Face metadata discovery/conversion handoff, drift-checked catalog-entry writing from manifest plus peer-offer proof, direct known-peer HTTP piece serve/fetch, one-command TinyRustLM peer-import request execution, and future broader P2P discovery/relay.
  - First local verifier implementation exists in `crates/minimodel-core` and `crates/minimodel`: manifest parse, boundary rejection, local artifact byte/SHA256 checks, TinyRustLM `.slm` validation, chunk/Merkle verification, `write-catalog-entry` proof validation, peer-piece export, direct HTTP peer-piece serving/fetch, peer-piece reassembly, `import-peer-request` receiver execution from TinyRustLM request JSON, and import receipt writing.
  - Local peer pieces are the first transfer bridge: `export-peer-pieces` writes `minimodel.peer_piece_set.v0` plus local chunk files from a verified `.slm`, `serve-peer-pieces` validates and serves only declared sidecar/piece files from a user-started direct HTTP listener, `fetch-peer-pieces` retrieves a piece set and chunks from a consenting direct `http://` peer while rejecting project-server hosts and checksum drift, `assemble-peer-pieces` reassembles only after piece SHA256 checks plus full artifact verification, and `import-peer-request` wraps the receiver sequence for TinyRustLM handoff JSON.
  - Real non-hosted q8 fixture metadata lives at `examples/tiny-test-model-q8.minimodel.manifest.v0`, `examples/tiny-test-model-q8.minimodel-peer-offer`, and generated `examples/catalog-entry.v0.json`; the `.slm` artifact remains outside MiniModel.org.
  - It references MiRust.com as a one-way talisman source.
  - File Handoff setup is initialized with placeholder-only active intake.
  - Public boundary remains no hosted model weights and no server-side inference.
